        "title": "Speech Act Theory: Austin and Searle",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Classical philosophy of language focused on declarative sentences and their truth conditions. But most language does not describe — it commands, promises, warns, greets, marries, declares war, fires employees. Austin observed that a theory focused on description misses the majority of what language actually does."
